description: Public-endpoint hardening rules for this platform
globs: app/api/**/*.ts,lib/**/*.ts,services/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security

- Every public route must validate with Zod before touching business logic.
- Public write endpoints (submissions) must set explicit CORS headers and echo/allowlist the Origin — never use wildcard `*` on submissions.
- Handle OPTIONS preflight explicitly on CORS-sensitive routes.
- Config delivery may be CORS-open; submissions must not be.
- Side effects that are not the primary write (email, webhooks) must be wrapped so they cannot throw past the handler.
- Admin queries for widgets/submissions must be scoped to the authenticated tenant from the session — never trust a client-supplied tenant id.
- Return honest 4xx status codes for bad shape (400), oversized (413/422), and rate limits (429). Do not paper over failures as 500.
